KG42.register("edges-27a4f8c7909e271a62a8e02d",{"id":"S-85407756a0221425","source":"KG31-623d45f464e9bce4","type":"limits","target":"KG31-a9bd9e360b96ff06","evidence_class":"S","scientific_acceptance":false,"relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"paper_ids":["11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation"],"assertions":[{"id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R002::E::v141-c-R002-E001","paper":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","rule_ref":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R002","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R002-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"bidding.supply","type":"limits","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E01","v141-b-g03-E04","v141-b-g03-E11"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002-C002"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"KG31-623d45f464e9bce4","target":"KG31-a9bd9e360b96ff06","source_occurrence_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R002::V::coordination.local_operator","target_occurrence_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R002::V::bidding.supply","source_unit_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-a-M01::coordination.local_operator","target_unit_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-a-M01::bidding.supply","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Optional bid-count step length control in iterative P2P energy bidding; selection covers all participants and applies to supply bids among their submissions. | Proposed practical coordinator enforcement of optional bid-ramping control in P2P energy bidding. | Supply energy-bid constraints in the simulation's iterative decision-making model. | Supply quantities represented within SDR energy bids during the iterative bidding process. | Supply-bid updates under optional combined step length control.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g03-E01","v141-b-g03-E02","v141-b-g03-E03","v141-b-g03-E04","v141-b-g03-E11","v141-b-g07-ev-04","v141-b-g07-ev-05","v141-b-g07-ev-11"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"ee57bc1c5eee580941af959fbed688006e3f22f354b26dd3352a816e4c868767","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"Requested quantities represented in the SDR energy-bid profile are submitted to the local coordinator at every iteration. Scope: SDR iterative submission of signed net-energy profiles within an energy sharing region. Condition: The submitted profile contains a nonnegative net-energy bid at the relevant time step. Offered quantities represented in the SDR energy-bid profile are submitted to the local coordinator at every iteration. Scope: SDR iterative submission of signed net-energy profiles within an energy sharing region. Condition: The submitted profile contains a negative net-energy bid at the relevant time step. The coordinator must provide and operate the trading platform and its associated metering mechanisms. Scope: Coordinator infrastructure obligations in the described local P2P framework. The coordinator does not control devices directly and applies unified rules fairly to all participants. Scope: Coordinator intervention under the paper's heuristic convergence techniques. Condition: When the heuristic techniques interfere with participants' control of their devices. Handling physical-network problems such as overvoltage and congestion is outside the coordinator's modeled remit and is deferred to further research. Scope: Limits of the coordinator's modeled remit in the studied P2P framework.","target_definition":"The coordinator limits supply-bid updates by evenly randomly selecting a predefined-size set of participants forbidden to change their energy bids at each iteration. Scope: Optional bid-count step length control in iterative P2P energy bidding; selection covers all participants and applies to supply bids among their submissions. Condition: Bid-count control is adopted; the supply bid belongs to a participant selected into the forbidden set. The coordinator must reject a supply bid whose change exceeds the prescribed ramping-rate limit. Scope: Proposed practical coordinator enforcement of optional bid-ramping control in P2P energy bidding. Condition: The proposed enforcement rule is adopted and a supply bid exceeds the prescribed ramping-rate limit. SDR supply bids follow the energy-bid content specification in Formula (A18), derived from the participant's decision-making-model results. Scope: Supply quantities represented within SDR energy bids during the iterative bidding process. Condition: The energy bid is negative at the relevant time step. Supply-bid changes at each iteration must respect the prescribed ramping allowance around the previous bid, with the resulting bounds clipped to the minimum and maximum energy-bid limits. Scope: Supply energy-bid constraints in the simulation's iterative decision-making model. Condition: The bid-ramping form of optional step length control is adopted. The two controls may be combined by first limiting the number of bids allowed to change and then limiting changes to the allowable supply bids. Scope: Supply-bid updates under optional combined step length control. Condition: Bid-count control and bid-ramping control are used together.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C001","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The coordinator limits supply-bid updates by evenly randomly selecting a predefined-size set of participants forbidden to change their energy bids at each iteration. Scope: Optional bid-count step length control in iterative P2P energy bidding; selection covers all participants and applies to supply bids among their submissions. Condition: Bid-count control is adopted; the supply bid belongs to a participant selected into the forbidden set.","expression":"e^{bid}_{i,j} = e^{bid}_{i-1,j},   j ∈ 𝓟𝓐^{forbid} ⊂ 𝓟𝓐   (9)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R002-x-01"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R002-th-forbid"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E01","v141-b-g03-E04","v141-b-g02-e23"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C002","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"The coordinator must reject a supply bid whose change exceeds the prescribed ramping-rate limit. Scope: Proposed practical coordinator enforcement of optional bid-ramping control in P2P energy bidding. Condition: The proposed enforcement rule is adopted and a supply bid exceeds the prescribed ramping-rate limit.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E11","v141-b-g02-e31"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E01","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p08-c1r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Y. Zhou et al. bid of the previous iteration with Δ = rmp ·|e ibid− 1 |. Besides, if the upper di bo","equation_id":"9","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The step length control can also be achieved by limiting the number of the bids allowed to be changed at each iteration. That is, e_{i,j}^{bid} = e_{i-1,j}^{bid}, j ∈ 𝓟𝓐^{forbid} ⊂ 𝓟𝓐 (9) where j is the index of prosumer agent. 𝓟𝓐^{forbid} is the set of prosumer agents who are forbidden to change their energy bids at the i th iteration. The number of the elements in 𝓟𝓐^{forbid}, i.e. |𝓟𝓐^{forbid}|, is pre-defined. During simulation, Formula (9) should be added to the decision-making model (as described by Formula (3)) of jth prosumer agent to make it function."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E04","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p08-c1r2__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"agents who are forbidden to change their energy bids at the i th itera- p tion. The number of the e","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"At each iteration, the elements of 𝓟𝓐^{forbid}, i.e. the prosumers who are forbidden to change their bids, are evenly randomly selected by the coordinator to ensure the fairness among prosumers. The number of prosumers forbidden affects the magnitude of energy and price change in the region at each iteration, thus potentially affecting the convergence performance."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E11","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p09-c1r2__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.3.3","anchor_text":"y g ( vergence obtained in this way may be far from the feasible optimum). ti th 3.3.3. Practical im","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The first technique, step length control, limits the ramping rate of the bids in the bidding process. In practice, this can be realised by the coordinator through setting bidding rules in the implementation model, as described in Section 3.2.4, in a P2P energy sharing mechanism. For example, the mechanism can achieve this by requiring that the coordinator should reject any bid that exceeds the prescribed ramping rate so that all the prosumers have to obey the ramping rate limit. Therefore, the step length control technique in simulation is able to suggest better bidding rules in the implementation model in practice."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e23","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p08-c1r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.3.1","anchor_text":"Y. Zhou et al. bid of the previous iteration with Δ = rmp ·|e ibid− 1 |. Besides, if the upper di bo","equation_id":"9","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The step length control can also be achieved by limiting the number of the bids allowed to be changed at each iteration. That is,\n   e^{\\mathrm{bid}}_{i,j} = e^{\\mathrm{bid}}_{i−1,j}    j \\in \\mathcal{PA}^{\\mathrm{forbid}} \\subset \\mathcal{PA}                                         (9)\nwhere j is the index of prosumer agent. \\mathcal{PA}^{\\mathrm{forbid}} is the set of prosumer agents who are forbidden to change their energy bids at the i th iteration. The number of the elements in \\mathcal{PA}^{\\mathrm{forbid}}, i.e. |\\mathcal{PA}^{\\mathrm{forbid}}|, is pre-deﬁned. During simulation, Formula (9) should be added to the decision-making model (as described by Formula (3)) of jth prosumer agent to make it function. ... At each iteration, the elements of \\mathcal{PA}^{\\mathrm{forbid}}, i.e. the prosumers who are forbidden to change their bids, are evenly randomly selected by the coordinator to ensure the fairness among prosumers."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e31","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p09-c1r2__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.3.3","anchor_text":"y g ( vergence obtained in this way may be far from the feasible optimum). ti th 3.3.3. Practical im","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In practice, this can be realised by the coordinator through setting bidding rules in the implementation model, as described in Section 3.2.4, in a P2P energy sharing mechanism. For example, the mechanism can achieve this by requiring that the coordinator should reject any bid that exceeds the prescribed ramping rate so that all the prosumers have to obey the ramping rate limit. Therefore, the step length control technique in simulation is able to suggest better bidding rules in the implementation model in practice."}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Optional bid-count step length control in iterative P2P energy bidding; selection covers all participants and applies to supply bids among their submissions. | Proposed practical coordinator enforcement of optional bid-ramping control in P2P energy bidding. | Supply energy-bid constraints in the simulation's iterative decision-making model. | Supply quantities represented within SDR energy bids during the iterative bidding process. | Supply-bid updates under optional combined step length control.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g03-E01","v141-b-g03-E02","v141-b-g03-E03","v141-b-g03-E04","v141-b-g03-E11","v141-b-g07-ev-04","v141-b-g07-ev-05","v141-b-g07-ev-11"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R002-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"bidding.supply","type":"limits","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E01","v141-b-g03-E04","v141-b-g03-E11"]},"paper_scope_note":"SDR, MMR, and BS are kept separate; the A18 net quantity differs from the A24 independent component; optional step-size control and the divergent loop in the example are not treated as general convergence or necessary dependencies."}}],"assertion_ids":["11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R002::E::v141-c-R002-E001"]});
